#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 82.46pt, "Figure 1. Plasmonic nanopores and optical probing strategies. (top) SEM images of representative conical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 96.98pt, "gold nanopores fabricated on thin membranes, showing reproducible tip morphology and nanoscale ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 111.5pt, "apertures at the center. Scale bars: 500 nm. (bottom) Schematic illustration of the two experimental ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 125.9pt, "configurations used in this work: DNA-PAINT imaging, where transient fluorescent events report local ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 140.42pt, "optical fields at the nanopore tips, and distance-dependent fluorescence measurements using DNA ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 154.94pt, "oligonucleotides of defined lengths (3 nm, 6 nm, 9 nm) acting as molecular nanorulers. Together, these ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 169.46pt, "approaches enable single-molecule mapping and quantitative analysis of plasmonic enhancement and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 183.86pt, "quenching within the confined near-field region. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 206.42pt, "In this work, we introduce DNA-PAINT and DNA-based nanorulers within plasmonic nanopores, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 220.82pt, "establishing a new approach to probe optical fields and surface functionality at the single-molecule level. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 235.34pt, "Fluorophores positioned at controlled distances from the metallic surface, through DNA oligos of different ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 249.86pt, "lengths, act as nanorulers to quantify how fluorophore-metal separation balances electromagnetic field ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 264.41pt, "enhancement and quenching. We find that the emission intensity follows a clear distance-dependent ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 278.81pt, "trend, with an optimal regime at intermediate spacing where enhancement dominates over non-radiative ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 293.33pt, "decay, in line with the typical maximum observed for emitters near gold nanospheres.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(479.86pt, 289.37pt, "23")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(486.82pt, 293.33pt, " In parallel, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 307.85pt, "transient DNA-PAINT binding events provide a dynamic optical readout localized at the nanopores, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 322.37pt, "confirming selective functionalization and spatially confined fluorescence, indicating areas of higher ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 336.89pt, "brightness corresponding to plasmonic hotspots. Finally, we extend the concept to dual-material ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 351.29pt, "nanopores, and achieve hybrid plasmonic–semiconducting structures by laterally combining gold and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 365.81pt, "silicon. The optical interaction between Au and Si at the nanoscale can itself enhance local fields,")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(513.34pt, 361.85pt, "24")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(520.3pt, 365.81pt, " and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 380.33pt, "such asymmetric architectures could enable diverse surface chemistries and multimodal operation, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 394.85pt, "opening a route toward multifunctional nanopore platforms. Figure 1 illustrates the architecture of the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 409.25pt, "plasmonic nanopores and the combined experimental approaches used in this work. Conical gold ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 423.77pt, "nanopores fabricated on thin membranes present well-defined apertures at the tip, where DNA docking ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 438.31pt, "strands are immobilized for single-molecule DNA-PAINT readout. Fluorophores positioned at defined ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 452.83pt, "distances via short, medium, and long DNA oligos (3, 6, 9 nm) act as nanorulers to probe near-field effects. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 467.23pt, "Together, these complementary strategies enable mapping of optical enhancement and quenching within ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 481.75pt, "the plasmonic nanopore geometry and establish the experimental framework for the results discussed ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 496.27pt, "below. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 15.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 527.47pt, "Results and discussion ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 543.79pt, "We first investigated how the fluorophore-metal separation distance influences emission strength in ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 558.31pt, "plasmonic nanopores by functionalizing identical pores with DNA oligonucleotides of three different ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 572.83pt, "lengths, therefore positioning the dyes at controlled separations from the metallic surface (Figure 2a).")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(533.26pt, 568.87pt, "25")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 587.35pt, "Each sample was prepared by the same surface chemistry and labeling protocol to ensure that only the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 601.78pt, "spacer length varied. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 624.34pt, "Using the three DNA spacers with different length, we observed a dependence of the fluorescence ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 638.74pt, "intensity on distance defined by the spacers in confocal microscopy as shown in Figure 2b-g (additional ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 653.26pt, "examples shown in Figure S1). The shortest linker (3 nm) produced weak emission, consistent with optical ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 667.78pt, "quenching by the metal; the intermediate 6 nm spacer maximized brightness, representing the regime ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 682.3pt, "where near-field enhancement dominates; and the longest 9 nm linker resulted in a slightly lower ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 696.696pt, "intensity, reflecting near-field decay with increasing separation.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(355.51pt, 692.736pt, "26 ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(363.91pt, 696.696pt, " Here, 3/6/9 nm denote nominal spacer ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 711.216pt, "lengths, and due to conformational tilting and flexibility the effective dye–metal separation is typically ")
]

