  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 82.46pt, "design window for optimizing optical response in metallic nanopores. These results highlight that emitters ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 96.98pt, "placed within an intermediate distance regime experience maximal enhancement, while those closer to ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 111.5pt, "the surface are dominated by non-radiative losses. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 133.94pt, "Finally, the introduction of dual-material Au/Si nanopores expands the concept toward multifunctional ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 148.46pt, "architectures. By combining plasmonic and semiconducting regions within a single conical geometry, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 162.86pt, "these structures offer simultaneous optical and electronic functionality, enabling tailored field ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 177.38pt, "distributions, selective chemistries, and potentially chiral optical responses. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 199.94pt, "Collectively, our results establish plasmonic nanopores as a powerful nanoscale platform for correlating ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 214.34pt, "optical fields, thermal effects, and molecular kinetics in confined geometries. The integration of DNA-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 228.86pt, "based probes provides a strategy to engineer and explore nanostructured interfaces with precision, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 243.38pt, "opening new directions for single-molecule sensing, plasmon-enhanced spectroscopy, and DNA data-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 257.93pt, "storage technologies. Future work will correlate fluorescence lifetime, local temperature, and ionic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 272.33pt, "conductance to fully map coupled optical-electrical effects in hybrid nanopores. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 15.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 326.09pt, "Experimental Methods ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 342.41pt, "Substrate and Nanopore Fabrication. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 364.97pt, "Three-dimensional oxide nanopores were fabricated on SiN/Si substrates by combining spin coating of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 379.37pt, "photoresist, focused ion beam (FIB) drilling, atomic layer deposition (ALD) of dielectric material (SiO₂ or ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 393.89pt, "Al₂O₃), and a final development step")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(244.85pt, 389.93pt, "10")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(251.81pt, 393.89pt, ". A 20 nm Au layer was then deposited to form a plasmonic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 408.41pt, "nanoantenna at the pore tip, with a 3-5 nm Cr or Ti adhesion layer between the dielectric and metal. Dual-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 422.93pt, "material nanopores were obtained by directional metal deposition: Au was evaporated at 90° to coat one ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 437.35pt, "side of the conical pores, followed by Si deposition after rotating the substrate 180°, yielding laterally ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 451.87pt, "asymmetric dielectric-plasmonic structures. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 474.43pt, "Surface Chemistry and Tip-Selective Functionalization. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 496.87pt, "Functionalization followed an established nanopore decoration protocol")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(437.59pt, 492.91pt, "12")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(444.55pt, 496.87pt, " adapted to DNA ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 511.39pt, "oligonucleotides in triethanolamine (TEA) buffer. Chips were plasma-activated for 5 min from the back ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 525.91pt, "(dielectric) side, TEA buffer was added to the top side, and a DNA-linker solution was applied on the back ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 540.31pt, "side. Docking strands or oligo nanorulers were incubated either overnight (DNA-PAINT) or briefly (0.5-2 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 554.83pt, "min) for distance-series labeling. Samples were rinsed in TEA buffer. Under these asymmetric conditions, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 569.35pt, "oligonucleotide attachment localized predominantly at the nanopore tip with negligible adsorption on the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 583.87pt, "surrounding flat substrate. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 606.34pt, "DNA-PAINT. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 628.78pt, "Docking strands (Table S1) were incubated overnight unless stated otherwise. Imaging strands were ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 643.3pt, "introduced during acquisition under standard PAINT conditions at concentrations between 50 pM and 50 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 657.82pt, "µM. Tip and base regions were imaged separately by shifting the focal plane 1-2 µm. Short-incubation ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 672.34pt, "tests (minutes) were performed for comparison with nanoruler experiments. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 694.776pt, "Imager: 5′-/Atto633N/AAGTTGTAATGAAGA/BHQ₂/-3′ ")
